From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: the Vulkan engine adapter

Kodi's side of the Vulkan engine (yblod-engine/vk, installed by the
yblod-engine-vk package with its header dv-engine-vk/dv_engine_vk.h):

- CDVPrivateVulkan loads the engine library at run time (dlopen of
  DV_VULKAN_ENGINE_LIBRARY or DVVK_LIBRARY, with an ABI check) and
  reports once when it cannot start. It submits each picture (the base
  and enhancement layers' decoded VAAPI surfaces, the metadata, the
  geometry and the output buffer), hands over Kodi's GUI framebuffer
  (read in place as a dma-buf, or copied as a fallback whose copies are
  made only when first needed), selects the output mode (Dolby Vision,
  HDR10 or HDR10+) and the engine options the settings ask for, and
  waits for the engine's tickets.
- CDVPrivateSource holds each decoded surface until the engine is done
  with it, plans the picture (CB1 Master Reference's processing for
  unscaled pictures with Annex B upscaling, chroma siting; the upscaler
  is latched for the life of an engine so siting and processing always
  agree), resets the engine when either layer's surface pool changes
  (so the engine runs with DVVK_SURFACE_CHECK=0), and recovers from an
  engine failure: drain, destroy, start again, twice without a thousand
  good frames in between, then the title goes back to plain playback.
  If the drain fails nothing is released, since the engine may still
  read the surfaces.
- A picture asked for again unchanged stays on screen: no submission
  and no commit for a pause or for the repeats of 24p on a 60 Hz mode
  (DV_PRIVATE_SKIP_REPEATS=0 renders every picture). The GUI buffer is
  handed to the engine only when GL wrote to it since
  (DV_PRIVATE_GUI_UNCHANGED_SKIP=0 hands it over every frame).
- CDVPrivateScanout and dv_scanout_slots: the linear 3840x2160 ARGB
  buffers the engine writes and their ownership (being written, ready,
  on screen, queued). dv_scanout_slots.cpp is Kodi's copy of
  yblod-engine/src/dv_scanout_slots.c. A third buffer exists only with
  queued flips (DV_PRIVATE_NONBLOCK=1).
- CDVPrivateDrain: the startup and end-of-stream waits for the first
  and last picture to be presented.

All new files, GPL-3.0-or-later as yblod-engine/LICENSE says for the
renderer's code. They use the metadata (kodi-9950), the settings
(kodi-9955) and the scanout plumbing (kodi-9953); kodi-9957 calls and
builds them.

Formerly the adapter parts of yblod-03 (native source), -15 (GUI
revision), -23 (Vulkan engine), -25 (CB1 Master Reference), -27
(engine sync), -29 (engine split), -30 (Vulkan only), -31, -32, -33
(bilinear EL), -34 (HDR10+), -42 to -49 (0.5.0 presentation rework),
-56, -59 and -60 (SPDX tags).
